  "result": "I added `split(cents, parts)` to `shop/money.py`, and all tests pass: the full suite ran 12 tests, 6 of them new.\n\nIt divides `cents` evenly, then gives one extra cent to each of the first parts until the remainder is used up. For example, `split(1000, 3)` gives `[334, 333, 333]`. A `parts` value below 1 raises `ValueError`.\n\nThe new tests are in `tests/test_money.py`. They cover an even split, the extra cents going to the first parts, more parts than cents (`split(2, 4)` gives `[1, 1, 0, 0]`), a single part, the totals always adding back up to `cents`, and the `ValueError` for 0 or negative parts.\n\nNegative amounts aren't tested. They still add up correctly, but the parts are uneven in a less obvious way: `split(-5, 2)` gives `[-2, -3]`. If refunds will use this, you may want the first part to get the larger negative amount instead.",
